  "platform": "Sega Mega Drive / Genesis",
  "summary": "Sonic & Knuckles is Sonic Team's platform adventure, released for Mega Drive on 18 October 1994.",
  "body": [
    "Sonic & Knuckles is Sonic Team's platform adventure, released for Mega Drive on 18 October 1994. Sonic pursues Doctor Robotnik and the Death Egg, while Knuckles faces a separate threat from EggRobo on Angel Island. Both characters run through zones filled with rings, springs and enemies, but their routes make different demands on the player. The game followed Sonic the Hedgehog 3 after the two projects had originally been planned together. Its cartridge also carried an unusual physical feature: a hinged slot for inserting another game.",
    "Sonic jumps higher and uses the abilities associated with the elemental shields. Knuckles trades that reach for gliding and climbing, allowing him to cross openings and scale walls that change the shape of his route. Those differences extend to the encounters and passages each character faces. A familiar-looking stretch can therefore require another approach when replayed with Knuckles. Maintaining speed remains useful, but choosing where to jump, glide or climb makes the landscape a set of possibilities rather than a single shared race to the exit.",
    "Connecting Sonic the Hedgehog 3 through the lock-on slot joins the two adventures into Sonic 3 & Knuckles, with their zones forming a longer journey. Connecting Sonic the Hedgehog 2 instead makes Knuckles playable in that earlier game. Other cartridges can lead to the Blue Sphere special-stage game. The connector turns a piece of cartridge hardware into part of the game's identity: an owner can place an existing game on top and discover a new use for it, with the combined third adventure offering the fullest version of the original plan."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Two routes across Angel Island",
    "A different way to climb",
    "A cartridge that opens"
  ],
